<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past month.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past month.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the month to July 4.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in month	 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Macquarie Bank	   12.40	25.89</p>
<p> 2  Burns,Philp &amp; Co	  2.42	22.22</p>
<p> 3  Email			 4.78	17.16</p>
<p> 4  Flc-Building Div	  4.07	16.92</p>
<p> 5  Publish Broadcst	  8.05	15.83</p>
<p> 6  National Mutual	   2.17	14.81</p>
<p> 7  Jupiters Ltd		3.48	14.47</p>
<p> 8  Commonwealth Bk	  16.06	13.02</p>
<p> 9  Harvey Norman	     7.90	12.86</p>
<p>10  News Corp		   6.50	12.85</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in month	 Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name		     Price	change</p>
<p> 1  Goldfields		  1.66     -23.15</p>
<p> 2  Acacia Resources	  1.61     -17.01</p>
<p> 3  Lihir Gold		  2.03     -13.62</p>
<p> 4  Plutonic Rsc		4.11     -13.58</p>
<p> 5  Normandy Min		1.41     -13.50</p>
<p> 6  Sthn Pac Pete	     4.10     -12.77</p>
<p> 7  RGC			   4.43     -12.28</p>
<p> 8  Sons Of Gwalia	    4.90	-9.26</p>
<p> 9  Great Central	     2.38	-7.67</p>
<p>10  CSL Limited		 7.85	-4.90</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
